      "content": "It's important to stress again that self-prescribing supplements based on generalized advice is risky. While some may start at high doses like 100-200 mg of iron per day, the effectiveness and safety of such a dosage can vary significantly from person to person. Excessive iron can potentially cause harm, leading to oxidative stress and damage to cells. Acute iron toxicity can be dangerous, and it's unsafe to push your limits without professional advice. The best way to address low iron levels quickly and safely is to consult with a healthcare provider who can tailor recommendations to your situation.",
